# The paged-media/core commit that the example-validation gate builds
# `paged-inspect` from (briefing §6.2 / §7 "docs version to the renderer's minor
# version"). Format: a single commit SHA on the first non-comment line.
#
# PIN POLICY: this pin tracks the LATEST core RELEASE TAG, not core@main. Bump it
# to the new tag's commit on every core release (e.g. v0.35.0 → the commit
# `git -C core rev-list -n1 v0.35.0` resolves to), via a deliberate PR. This keeps
# the docs gate building paged-inspect from the exact engine the published
# @paged-media packages ship from — so a validated example is one a released
# renderer accepts, never a main-only or pre-release one. The weekly core-drift job
# may surface a newer green main, but the pin only moves when a release is cut.
#
# Currently: v0.70.1 (tag commit 172d652). A renderer patch on v0.70.0: an
# oval's or polygon's object shadow is cast from what it paints (an unfilled
# shape from its stroke; a stroked oval as an ellipse with the stroke's outer
# half), measured against InDesign 2025. No wire change. All four packages
# answer at 0.70.1 on the registry (`latest`).
#
# v0.70.0 (tag commit 9bc22c2). Two protocol versions on from
# v0.68.0. Protocol 69 (v0.69.0, the data-publishing batch): fields at the
# caret, document-scoped plugin labels (`setDocumentMetadata`), pages a merge
# can make. Protocol 70: pages and masters for presentations (`movePage`,
# `setPageMetadata`, page links, snapshots without items, master editing and
# create/delete/rename; ADR 129) and the platform doors for plugin content
# (scene-layer scoped fonts, a handle on every batch mint, drop shadows on
# every shape; ADR 130). All four packages (canvas-wasm, introspect-wasm, sdk,
# idml-viewer) answer at 0.70.0 on the registry (`latest`), checked before this
# pin moved; core's own CI was green on the tag commit.
#
# v0.68.0 (tag commit c7c16a7). Two protocol versions on from
# v0.66.0 (v0.67.0 was released while this pin stayed put). Protocol 67 moves
# snapping into the engine (requestSnapPoint, setSnapSettings; ADR 125).
# Protocol 68 draws scene-layer text in its own face: a run's family plus
# weight/italic resolve through the host-registered fonts, the default face only
# as a fallback, reported on the reply as `fontFallbacks` (ADR 126). All four
# packages (canvas-wasm, introspect-wasm, sdk, idml-viewer) answer at 0.68.0 on
# the registry (`latest`), checked before this pin moved.
#
# v0.66.0 (tag commit fcffd2d). Two protocol versions on from v0.64.0
# (v0.65.0 was released while this pin stayed put). Protocol 65 widened the
# write surface: duplicateElements, stroke alignment and effects on every kind
# that draws them, opacity and blend on groups, paragraphComposer, a style's
# settable properties and a story's grow rule readable. Protocol 66 adds a pen
# path's end cap and line ends, the gradient axis read back on paths and ovals,
# rotate/scale/shear about a given point, a text frame's glyphs as outlines,
# plugin metadata on every scene-tree node, binary scene images and part bytes,
# `DeletePagedPart`, `deleteTable`, exact table undo, and per-page scene
# invalidation. All four packages (canvas-wasm,
# introspect-wasm, sdk, idml-viewer) answer at 0.66.0 on the registry (`latest`),
# checked before this pin moved; core's own CI was green on the tag commit.
#
# v0.64.0 (tag commit 6dea692): protocol 64 makes a batch of attributes the
# model already carried SETTABLE on the wire: `setFlowGrowRule` (a story's frame chain may grow, ADR 026, with
# copyFrameOptions per ADR 029), keep options and StartParagraph (the
# break-before rule, ADR 028), span and split columns (SpanColumnType), and the
# list-marker attributes. Rendering also moved: forced line breaks (U+2028),
# list-marker placement and character styles, text-frame StrokeAlignment insets.
# All four packages (canvas-wasm, introspect-wasm, sdk, idml-viewer) answer at
# 0.64.0 on the registry (`latest`), checked before this pin moved. NOTE core's
# own `ci` was red at the tag (its pdf export-diff lane, on the new list
# fixtures) — a CI-only lane, not a shipped-package defect; core main is green
# again after it.
#
# v0.63.0 made the SCRIPT BUDGET a wire parameter: `ExecuteScript` carries
# an optional `ScriptBudgetWire`, absent meaning the engine's own ceilings (the
# editor's 2 s REPL guard, unchanged) and `wallClockMs: 0` meaning no deadline.
#
# v0.63.0 also carries two fixes the docs gate cares about: `paged.set(id,
# "itemLayer", …)` actually WRITES now (protocol 62 taught the catalog to parse
# the path and the wire to apply it, and never taught `js_value_to_wire` it was
# string-valued, so it returned false and wrote nothing — a806321), and the
# directional feather paints the real coverage mask shared with the PDF lane
# rather than stamping a white blurred path (72cd7b3).
#
# v0.62.0 added `itemLayer` (assign an EXISTING page item to a layer — until
# protocol 62 layer membership was birth-only, settable in a paged-gen fixture
# and nowhere else), `UnlinkFrames.restore_target`, and the render-effect
# sweep's fixes: eleven operations that the wire accepted and reported success
# for while changing nothing on the page.
#
# Why the policy says "a tag whose packages are PUBLISHED", not just "a tag":
# the pin once named v0.51.2, a tag that was cut but never shipped — its release,
# and v0.51.1 and v0.51.0 before it, all died on an expired NPM_TOKEN that npm
# reported as a 404. The gate was then building paged-inspect from an engine no
# published package shipped from, which is exactly what this pin exists to prevent.
# v0.61.0 ended that gap; v0.63.0 is verified the same way — all four packages
# (canvas-wasm, introspect-wasm, sdk, idml-viewer) answer at 0.63.0 on the
# registry. Check that before moving this pin, not after. NOTE the v0.63.0
# publish took two attempts: the first was stopped by core's own subset audit
# because `paged-sdk` had come to link `paged-mutate` transitively, and npm
# answered PUT 202 (queued) rather than 200 for two of the four packages, so
# they read 0.62.0 for a few minutes after a green run. Both are reasons to
# check the registry rather than the workflow's conclusion.
#
# The WebGPU live preview does not build from this commit — it consumes the
# published npm `@paged-media/idml-viewer` at the matching release (its bundled
# wasm), so this pin governs the CI example/scripting gates only.
172d65238ddf2725f6c868d5dc1814393c1955eb
